# ── Supabase ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The standalone runs on its own project. At integration these become GomaAI's.
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=https://<project-ref>.supabase.co
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=
SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=

# ── App ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Absolute, no trailing slash. Becomes the deep link inside every reminder,
# so a wrong value fails silently — src/lib/env.ts validates it at boot.
APP_PUBLIC_URL=http://localhost:3000

# Bearer secret for POST /api/cron/process-reminders. Generate with:
#   node -e "console.log(require('crypto').randomBytes(32).toString('hex'))"
CRON_SECRET=

# ── WhatsApp (platform notifications number) ────────────────────────────────
# Same variable names as GomaAI, so integration needs no credential change.
# Nothing is delivered until client_event_reminder is APPROVED on this WABA.
GOMA_NOTIFY_PHONE_NUMBER_ID=
GOMA_NOTIFY_ACCESS_TOKEN=
GOMA_NOTIFY_WABA_ID=

# There is deliberately NO variable for the dialable number.
#
# There was one, briefly, and it was wrong within a day: it held
# +1 951-456-4663 while Meta's actual number was +1 951-456-4463. Nothing
# caught it, because nothing read it — and that is the whole problem with
# storing a number by hand next to the id that addresses it. Meta owns this
# fact, so GET /api/v1/whatsapp asks Meta for it (display_phone_number) rather
# than trusting a value somebody typed once.

# ── WhatsApp webhook (POST/GET /api/webhooks/whatsapp) ─────────────────────
# TWO DIFFERENT SECRETS. Meta's setup screen shows them together, which is why
# they get swapped, and swapping them fails in a way that looks like neither.
#
# VERIFY TOKEN: invent it, then type the SAME string into Meta's "Verify token"
# box. Used once, on the GET handshake. Rotate it freely afterwards — it
# authenticates nothing after subscription.
GOMA_NOTIFY_VERIFY_TOKEN=

# APP ID: Meta's numeric id for the APP, at App Settings -> Basic, sitting right
# above the app secret. Not the WABA id and not the phone number id — a third
# identity. Only needed so Settings -> WhatsApp can run the callback-URL
# verification itself; with APP ID + APP SECRET, Graph answers a failed
# handshake with a numbered reason, where the dashboard says only "The callback
# URL or verify token couldn't be validated" for every possible cause.
GOMA_NOTIFY_APP_ID=

# APP SECRET: issued by Meta, at App Settings -> Basic -> App secret. It is the
# HMAC key for X-Hub-Signature-256 on every POST, and it is the ONLY thing
# proving a payload came from Meta. Without it the route answers 503 and
# refuses every event, deliberately: this endpoint writes to `reminders`, so
# accepting unsigned bodies would let anyone who knows the URL mark real
# reminders failed.
GOMA_NOTIFY_APP_SECRET=

# Set to 1 to log what WOULD be sent and stamp a synthetic message id, so the
# whole pipeline is exercisable before Meta approves the template.
# Refused at boot when the runtime is production.
REMINDER_DRY_RUN=1

# ── AI (the one model call: drafting the suggested opener) ──────────────────
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
# Used only as the capacity fallback when Anthropic returns 429/529.
OPENAI_API_KEY=

# ── Runtime ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Set this on a laptop. isProductionRuntime() in src/lib/env.ts FAILS CLOSED —
# anything that is not explicitly "development" or "test" counts as production,
# because the alternative is a bare worker process quietly treating itself as
# dev and sending real messages. `next dev` sets NODE_ENV for you; the CLI
# scripts (tick, preflight, seed) run under tsx and do not, so without this
# they refuse to start while REMINDER_DRY_RUN is on.
APP_ENV=development
